	BUILD_LIBRESSL and BUILD_LIBWEBSOCKETS ON for each of them that is
	not found in /opt/musl or /opt/diet (or CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH), so it is
	built from source instead of picking up a host glibc copy.  A value
	given on the command line is kept.

	* cmake/BuildLibwebsockets.cmake (build_libwebsockets): New option
	BUILD_LIBRESSL.  When ON, LibreSSL is always built with
	build_libressl() (static, -fPIC when the libwebsockets build feeds a
	shared module) and libwebsockets is built against it, skipping the
